---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config';
---
<Base
  title="About, disclaimer and corrections"
  description="Who publishes this site, its independence from Harvard University, and how to request a correction."
  eyebrow="About"
  lede="An independent reference on what public records show about donor influence and institutional access at Harvard University."
  reviewed="2026-11-20"
>
  <h2 id="disclaimer">Non-affiliation disclaimer</h2>
  <p><strong>{site.disclaimerLong}</strong></p>
  <p>
    This is not the website of the Harvard Alumni Association or of any alumni club. Harvard’s official alumni site is
    alumni.harvard.edu. The site does not use Harvard’s shield, seal, colours or typefaces, and it does not solicit
    donations, membership or personal information.
  </p>

  <h2 id="purpose">Purpose</h2>
  <p>
    Universities publish a great deal about themselves. Official reviews, court filings and document releases are
    harder to find and to read together. This site gathers that record on one subject so that prospective students,
    students, alumni and researchers can read it in one place, with the strength of each source made visible.
  </p>
  <p>It takes no position on what any reader should conclude about the University or any person named.</p>

  <h2 id="who">Publisher</h2>
  <p>
    Published by {site.publisher}. The site carries no advertising and receives no funding from Harvard University or
    from any person or organisation discussed on it.
  </p>

  <h2 id="corrections">Corrections policy</h2>
  <p>
    If something here is wrong, incomplete or unfair, write to
    <a href={`mailto:${site.correctionsEmail}`}>{site.correctionsEmail}</a>. Please include the page, the sentence, and
    a public source we can check.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Every request is read. Requests from people named on the site are handled first.</li>
    <li>Confirmed errors are corrected on the page and recorded in the <a href="/updates/">update log</a> with a description of what changed.</li>
    <li>A person or institution discussed here may send a response for inclusion. Responses are added alongside the relevant passage.</li>
    <li>Material is removed where it cannot be supported by a public source at grade A2 or above.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="people">A note on people named</h2>
  <p>
    Many people appear in the underlying records for ordinary reasons: they received a gift, attended a meeting, or
    were mentioned in someone else’s email. Appearing in a document, or on this site, is not evidence of wrongdoing.
    Where an institution has made a finding about a person, the finding is quoted and attributed. Where it has not,
    the site says so.
  </p>

  <h2 id="legal">Use of names and marks</h2>
  <p>
    “Harvard” and related names are trademarks of the President and Fellows of Harvard College. They are used here
    only to identify the institution under discussion. Quotations are brief and attributed. Links to third-party sites
    are provided for verification, and this site is not responsible for their content.
  </p>
</Base>
